invariant: INV-17
file: aes_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aes-equiv
reason: the arm64 key expansion returns without wiping the word it copies
  each word of the schedule into, so its last value, a word of the last
  round key, stays in the dead frame after the call. Under a
  SUITE=aesgcm build that key is a traffic key. Every schedule is still
  right, so no vector notices. bin/aes_equiv_test clears the stack below
  a call, makes one expansion and looks for any word the expansion
  computed in the bytes the call wrote. Only an arm64 compiler reads the
  line, so the script builds that binary for arm64 and runs it under
  qemu-aarch64.

--- old
    ct_wipe(word, sizeof word);
    ct_wipe(substituted, sizeof substituted);
--- new
    ct_wipe(substituted, sizeof substituted);
